title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it could be used to foreshadow one of the themes of the chronicle, provide a hint for the character's own advancement or help drive home the philosophy that magic is alive. So what are you trying to setup with this scene ? How do you want it to echo at a later part in the story ?</div> </div> </div> </div>the primary goal is to use Forces to highlight how magic is alive, as will be my goal with all of these moments (at least as to how I've decided currently, future plans may change that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T16:33:03-07:00","id":1525043,"title":"","content":"Perhaps you could do something like the <a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Loveless\" target=\"_blank\">Loveless </a>poem from <i>Crisis Core</i>\u200b, a metaphorical guide that would lead them to greater Mysteries. If the passage they read is resonant with some events that are on top of mind, you could use the rest of the fragment as a clue that leads to a Mystery related to living Forces, such as a being akin to an <a href=\"https://xcom.fandom.com/wiki/Codex_(XCOM_2)\" target=\"_blank\">XCOM2 Codex</a>, created when a powerful imprint was made on data.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T12:00:07-08:00","id":1525129,"title":"","content":"The Mysterium splat-book states that &quot;The last rote to be found [in Corpus Mysteriorum] was a version of \u201cCall Lightning.\u201d It used metaphors that could only be understood after studying advances in plasma physics that arose after 1928.&quot; It's a cool tidbit that shows that the Corpus Author may have included knowledge that at the time of writing was centuries ahead of schedule.<br /> <br /> She also seems to have been fond of puzzles, like creating Runes within negative space of her writing. She could have also made some pages into Magic Eye pictures, or other sort of mundane illusions. Some fragments of text may reveal new information when read backwards, upside-down, or in a mirror. Look into ambigrams and ambigram art for examples.<br /> <br /> An idea I'm personally fond of is to mention various stellar bodies sending messages through their radiation. The Universe's greatest example of Forces being alive in some sense. You can also look into what unusual Skills your players favor, and have some pages of the Grimoire address Forces through those Skill's lens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}